what's going on guys today we're going  through the top 10 moments from my  academia's war arc which is seemingly  concluded in the manga  after over a year's worth of chapters  the 10 moments i've chosen for this  video are my personal favorites  but there are of course many other  things that did happen that are great  but they just didn't make the cut  just before we get into it be sure to  sub to the channel if you haven't  already  and let me know what your top three  moments were from this arc down below  okay so the first moment we're going to  talk about is the initial raid  on the paranormal liberation front  mansion this scene felt like something  straight out of an avengers movie  as you had a ton of pro heroes and  students going all  out against the villains with many  characters putting in their best ever  performance  cementos managed to single-handedly  split the front of the mansion in two  tokoyami took down reed destro at least  you know temporarily  and kaminari saved all the frontline  heroes from his father  okay it wasn't really his father but it  was a guy with a powerful electricity  type quirk  and kamino just absorbed all his attacks  like it was nothing  we also saw the beginning of hawke's  betrayal of twice  which was not only a great fight but it  was actually really emotional seeing  twice his regret  at having trusted hawks overall i'd rate  the beginning of the raid as  certified peak fiction hence why it's in  my top 10 moments  next up the reveal of kurogiri's true  identity was something that occurred at  the beginning of the arc  and this was special for a lot of  reasons as a reader of my academia  vigilantes  finding out that kurogiri was actually  shirokumo was a  crazy plot twist because shirakuma used  to be a student at ua  alongside izawa and present mike  shirakumo's supposed death  is what turned izawa into the character  he is today so to find out that his body  was harvested  and then turned into a villain that  we've known since season 1  yeah that's a pretty big deal aizawa had  a mix of both sadness and disgust upon  finding out this information  but perhaps the best thing about this  reveal was shirakumo  briefly overriding his nomu programming  to give the heroes a clue that would  help them locate shigaraki  this straight up proves that there is  still a little bit of the real shirokumo  left inside  so do any of you guys think he might  return as a hero in the future  with erie being a thing surely it's not  totally impossible  in eighth place we have mirko versus the  hyena nomus  which was a valiant effort from the  rabbit hero to stop shigeraki from  waking up  in truth there were more heroes than  just mirko who took on the nomus  but she was the first one to arrive in  the lab where shigaraki was  and she went up against a gang of high  ends by herself  for what was probably about five minutes  or so seeing this happen from week to  week was very exciting  as we kept wondering whether the heroes  would actually be able to stop shigaraki  in time  at some moments it looked like mirko  would be able to deal with the nomu  but then in other moments it seemed like  she was ready to accept her death  even after she finally made it to the  tank where shiguraki was  it still wasn't enough to stop the  villain president mike obviously was  able to finish off the job  but we all know how things went after  that onto seventh place  this spot goes to izuka midoriya  unlocking his third quark  during the battle against shigaraki this  moment came after shiguraki was about to  touch the ground and kill everyone with  decay  but deku used black whip to grab the  heroes before shooting off into the sky  thanks to his new quirk  which is called float what was really  iconic was that he used black whip to  also pull shigaraki into the air as well  before telling the villain up here is  where i'll beat you  there are very few moments in the series  in which deku has been cooler than this  i mean he's got a new quirk he saved  everyone's life  and he's boldly threatening the person  who just gave the number one hero a good  beat down  float was the perfect counter to  shigaraki's decay and without  it who knows what would have happened  moving on we have the death of twice  which occurred after hawke stabbed him  in the back both literally  and metaphorically whilst talks was  undercover with the league of villains  he and twice became very good friends  almost to the point where you could  forget  that hawk still was on the hero side  however at the start of the war  hawks betrayed twice without any  hesitation so that he couldn't use his  double quirk against the heroes  it was at this moment that we learnt how  cold hawks really is  as he basically made fun of twice for  believing his act  that final scene of twice's clone  returning to toga before melting away  it was nothing short of fantastic and i  don't think harikoshi could have handled  twice's death much better than this  even though twice was the one who ended  up dying it could have very easily been  hawks instead if dabi was more efficient  with his flames  in fifth place we have a moment that was  short and sweet but it was still one of  my favorite things to happen during the  war  ashigaraki was beating down the heroes  it became clear that even with his  quirks erased  he was still virtually near all might  levels of power  this meant that shigaraki with just two  fingers was able to flick a quote-string  bullet towards izawa  as if it was being fired from a weapon  however without any hesitation  the professor whips out his support item  before cutting the bottom half of his  leg clean off  isabella did this so fast that the quote  destroying bullet didn't even have time  to erase his quirk and even shigaraki  had to admit  this was a pretty cool move i personally  know i would never have done the same  thing in that same situation  so kudos to azawa for being that awesome  the fourth best moment in the war arc  was the surprise return of lemilian  which really came out of nowhere  but in a way that's what made it so hype  absolutely  nobody was expecting him to return when  he did clearly not even deku  so for lemelian to appear on the  battlefield it almost felt like a gift  from harukoshi  the way i see it with all the heroes  that have died this arc such as cross  for example  i feel like muriel returning out of  nowhere is kind of meant to compensate a  little bit  for all the heroes that have been lost  after all izawa did say that muriel had  potential to be the next number one hero  so yeah he's clearly a massive asset now  moving on to my personal top three  moments from mikey academia's war arc  the third best moment came in chapter  285  and it was yeah it was pretty iconic at  this point all for one had taken over  shiguraki's body temporarily  which by itself was already pretty cool  as afo went to attack midoriya with  force quick activation  bakugo's body moves without thinking and  he activates a new condensed form of  explosion  that are faster and stronger than  anything he's done before  these new explosions enabled him to  reach midoriya in time  and push him out of the way but in the  process bakago himself  got skewered by all for one this wasn't  like when afo  harmlessly used force quick activation  on kirigiri  instead these tentacles went straight  through bakugou's body  causing major internal damage when this  chapter came out we had no idea what was  going to happen next  i remember there was speculation in the  comments about whether afo would steal  back and go's quirk  or whether back and go might die and  while neither of those things ended up  happening  it was still super exciting waiting for  the next chapter i cannot imagine bakago  from season 1  sacrificing himself in this way so this  scene really cemented  his development into what all might  would describe as a true hero  the second best moment of the arc was  when shiguraki finally woke up  after the heroes did pretty much  everything they could to stop that from  happening  we got that amazing dream sequence in  which he walks towards afo and inherits  the all for one quirk  followed by shigaraki waking up and  immediately wiping out  thousands of people with just one hand  shiki turned most of the city to dust  killing the number 6 hero crossed as  well as many other innocents in the  process  his new and improved decay quirk had  several upgrades which i spoke about in  a different video  and by the time it was finished only a  stump of ground remained of the hospital  this moment was jaw-dropping like we saw  heroes being  dusted in the streets we saw civilians  who were clearly about to be dusted  it was just it's completely nuts of  course once the destruction was complete  then we got to see shigeraki  show off his new quirks against  endeavour and yeah that was pretty cool  too  with that said before we move on to my  personal favorite moment of the war arc  the honorable mentions for this video  include best genus still being alive  mr compresses past being revealed  kirishima getting the sedative into  giganto marquia's mouth  and gigantomachia destroying many many  cities on his way to shigeraki  okay so the main event is something so  epic  that when this bull is dropped for this  it trended higher than the 2020 us  election  that is not a joke i will link to the  article in the description but yeah  these spoilers dropped in early november  during the middle of the u.s election  and still despite that derby was the  main trending topic which is  honestly one of the funniest things i've  ever seen of course the reason for that  was that in chapter 219  i can't even of course the reason for  that was that in chapter 290  debbie was revealed to be toyo todoroki  who was the long lost son of endeavor  and the brother of shoto most of us  suspected that he was toyo todoroki  but to have it confirmed beyond any  reasonable doubt it was just an amazing  feeling like we've been waiting for so  long it was just really satisfying  seeing the reaction of the todoroki  family not to mention getting more  details on toya's backstory  and witnessing the downfall of endeavour  all at once  yeah that's just ridiculous dabi's hair  being white was also the icing on the  cake  as now there is a clear distinction  between the debbie era of the series  and the toya era of the series going  forward after the reveal of his identity  toyo went on an insane rampage trying to  kill endeavour with prominence burn  then attacking nedjaray before finally  attempting to kill  shoto from the dialogue we could tell  that toya is now a lost cause  because he just has no feelings for  anyone and even natsuo who was his  favorite sibling he didn't even care if  he died  overall the debbie reveal was basically  everything i wanted it to be  but let me know your thoughts on that  down below and of course let me know  your top three moments from the war arc  as well  thanks for watching as always and if you  enjoyed this video then be sure to hit  that like button because it will help  other people find the video  until the next one peace out

